<script>
  import IsoFigure from "#lib/ui/IsoFigure.svelte";
  // FIG. 2 of the oil and gas page (2026-11-24; FIG. 4 for its first hour): one field, one list in the morning. The founder's ask
  // of 2026-11-24, a macro view beside the bench (FIG. 1) and the pipe (FIG. 2). A field from above in
  // the isometric hand: two platforms offshore, four wells on pumps, a tank battery with a truck at its
  // load line, a compressor station, the service yard and the office, with the Wave console in front of
  // it. The use case is exception-based surveillance: every site writes its records all night, the
  // model reads them together, and the morning list says where a person goes first and why. A quiet
  // well stays off the list. The scrubbed list under the stage plays it: 1 the night, every site's way
  // into the console carries a comet; 2 to 5 the morning list, one site lights and lifts and the route
  // from the yard's gate runs to it (by the dock and across the water for the platform). The pump
  // beams nod (transform only, none under reduced motion).
  //
  // The drawing between the markers is generated by computer-scientist/article/fig_field_gen.py (one
  // camera and one hand with FIG. 1 and FIG. 2, isolib.py; the console is isoparts.console). Same
  // contract as UseCaseFigure.svelte: runes, no <style> (oil-gas.css, lead .ff), no colour literal, no
  // inline style, every word in HTML, no SVG <text>, role="group" named by its caption, data-draw.
  // Still (no JS, print, reduced motion): step 1, the night.
  //
  // Nothing here is a result: the list is a design for a custom tuning on a field's own records, and
  // the section above the figure says so.
  let {
    fig = 2,
    caption = "One field from above: two platforms offshore, wells on pumps, a tank battery, a compressor station, the service yard and the office where the model runs. Every site's records come in overnight. In the morning the list says where a person goes first, and why. A quiet site stays off it.",
    stops = [
      { key: "night", name: "Overnight", note: "every site's records come in", reads: "Pump cards, tank gauges, alarms and daily reports in, all night" },
